WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.538
Hi! Is the cat on the table or under it? Is a birthday on Monday or in May? Today we'll learn prepositions for places and times.

2
00:00:11.688 --> 00:00:16.410
In means inside, on means on top of and touching, under means below.

3
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:23.514
Between is in the middle of two things, next to is beside, behind is at the back, and in front of is ahead.

4
00:00:23.664 --> 00:00:27.426
At is for a point, like at the bus stop or at school.

5
00:00:27.576 --> 00:00:33.330
For movement: jump into the pool, walk across the road.

6
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.698
Use at for clock times: at 7 o'clock, and at night.

7
00:00:37.848 --> 00:00:41.370
Use on for days, dates and special days.

8
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.834
Use in for months, years, and parts of the day like the morning.

9
00:00:45.984 --> 00:00:55.218
A trick: the smallest, clock times, use at; days use on; the biggest, months and years, use in.

10
00:00:55.368 --> 00:00:59.658
Watch out! We don't use in before days of the week!

11
00:00:59.808 --> 00:01:03.450
Days and dates take on: on Monday, on 5 May.

12
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.122
Months take in: in May.

13
00:01:07.272 --> 00:01:16.794
Your turn! The keys are, ___, the drawer. In, on or at? Pause and think.

14
00:01:16.944 --> 00:01:22.626
The keys are inside the drawer, so in. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:22.776 --> 00:01:32.322
Another one! We have PE, ___, Tuesday. Which one? Pause and think.

16
00:01:32.472 --> 00:01:37.530
Days of the week take on. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:48.522
Here's another! School starts, ___, 7.30 a.m. Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:48.672 --> 00:01:53.634
Clock times take at. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:53.784 --> 00:02:03.906
Try one more! The ball is, ___, the two boxes. Which one? Pause and think.

20
00:02:04.056 --> 00:02:09.858
In the middle of two boxes: between. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:10.008 --> 00:02:20.826
Try one more! Grandpa was born, ___, 1960. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:20.976 --> 00:02:25.506
Years take in. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:25.656 --> 00:02:35.346
Try one more! The cat is hiding, ___, the bed. Which one? Pause and think.

24
00:02:35.496 --> 00:02:40.770
Hiding below the bed: under. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:50.466
Last one! We go swimming, ___, the morning. Which one? Pause and think.

26
00:02:50.616 --> 00:02:56.154
Parts of the day take in: in the morning. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:56.304 --> 00:03:05.010
Remember: prepositions tell us place and time. Use at for clock times, on for days and dates, and in for months and years.

28
00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:10.097
Say where your school bag is, using a preposition!

